<Layout title="About | Carrie Feng">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p style="margin-top:18px;">
    I’m interested in how climate, data, and communication intersect in real life. A lot of environmental issues feel distant or abstract, and I like working on ways to make them more concrete. That often means using data analysis or GIS to translate large systems into something people can see, question, and act on.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top:18px;">
    I’m also really drawn to product storytelling, especially in design and brand development. I think a lot about how sustainability is communicated, how consumers interpret those messages, and where data can either clarify or complicate the story. I’m curious about the space between what brands say and what their data actually shows, and how design and narrative shape trust.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top:14px;">
    Outside of academics, I like projects that involve observing and documenting. I enjoy traveling, photography, ceramics, and lately picked up running. I’m someone who likes both structure and experimentation, whether that’s building a visualization or simply sketching out an idea.

More generally, I’m motivated by curiosity and impact. I like learning across disciplines, asking a lot of questions, and working on things that connect environmental systems with everyday human experience.
  </p>
</Layout>
